{
  "id": 1001,
  "name": "Copy new Postgres orders into Google Sheets",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nRuns every morning at 06:00, reads the orders that have not been exported yet from Postgres, appends them to a Google Sheet, and then marks each exported row with `exported_at`.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Add a **Postgres** credential and point the queries at your own table.\n2. Add a **Google Sheets** credential, select your spreadsheet in the **Document** control, and select the **Orders** sheet in the **Sheet** control.\n3. Adjust the schedule if 06:00 is not the right time for you, then activate the workflow.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe final Postgres node only marks a row after the sheet append succeeds. If the append succeeds but the update fails, a later run can still duplicate that row; use a transaction or an outbox pattern for a production integration.",
